# Quest for Ancient Secrets: "Remove five quest counters from this enchantment and sacrifice it: Target player shuffles
# their graveyard into their library." Two Thought Scours on Bot1 put six cards into its graveyard, so six counters.
# After the first (three counters) the ability cannot be activated: its five counters are not there (the refusal, with
# the activation after the second as its positive control). Activated targeting Bot1, the sacrifice is a cost (CR 118.3),
# so Quest itself is in the graveyard when the ability resolves and is shuffled in with the rest (CR 701.24a): the
# graveyard ends empty, the library holds all of it, and Quest is no longer on the battlefield. Quest is not on the
# battlefield to see itself go into the graveyard, so Bot1 is asked nothing for it (the closing refusal).

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Quest for Ancient Secrets
Thought Scour
Thought Scour
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x21

